[statement]
A package whose condition's `!` entry forbids a package the walk has
reached, placed or still being walked, is not walked where the placement
of a package its condition names triggers it: placing `pa` would trigger
`plug`, whose condition is `pa !pw`, but `pw`, which needs `pa`, is being
walked. `plug` is placed where `need` reaches it, after `x` and `y`.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:pw x y need

P:pw
V:1
D:pa

P:pa
V:1

P:x
V:1

P:y
V:1

P:plug
V:1
D:lib
i:pa !pw

P:lib
V:1

P:need
V:1
D:plug

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install pa 1
install pw 1
install x 1
install y 1
install lib 1
install plug 1
install need 1
install app 1
